[h1]Detailed Map Tacks Tweaks by Najane[/h1]

An [b]add-on[/b] for [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3507297712][b]Detailed Map Tacks[/b] by wltk[/url]. It changes two things about how map tacks behave. Both are optional and both can be switched off.

[b]It is not a replacement and it does nothing on its own.[/b] Detailed Map Tacks is required, and this mod declares it as a hard dependency - if that mod is missing or switched off, this one quietly does not apply rather than filling your log with errors.

[h2]What it changes[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]A generic map tack disappears once something that fulfils it is built.[/b] Detailed Map Tacks clears a tack when the building it names is finished on that tile, but it compares the two type names as text - so only a tack for one specific building ever matches. A "culture building", "wonder" or "improvement" tack has no single name to match and stays on the map. This clears it using the same list of buildings the tack's own tooltip already shows you, plus the game's type tags for civ-unique buildings.
[*] [b]Right-click a map tack on the map to delete it.[/b] On its own, Detailed Map Tacks deletes a tack on left-click and only while the tack chooser is open - its source carries wltk's own "TODO: Come up with a better quicker deletion solution." The click is swallowed, so deleting a tack does not also send your selected unit walking to that tile.
[/list]

Walls and other slotless buildings do not clear a tack, and a unique quarter tack waits for both of its buildings: a plan is only cleared once it is genuinely finished.

[h2]Options[/h2]
Both live under a [b]Detailed Map Tacks[/b] heading in [b]Options - Mods[/b], so there is one place to look for map tack settings:
[list]
[*] [b]Apply Najane's changes[/b] (on by default) - turns everything this mod does off without uninstalling it. The first thing to try if map tacks start behaving oddly after a Detailed Map Tacks update.
[*] [b]Remove map tacks with right-click[/b] (on by default).
[/list]

[h2]For wltk[/h2]
These are [b]suggestions, not corrections[/b] - whether a generic tack should clear at all is a design call, and the deletion shortcut is the note you already left yourself. [b]If you want either change in Detailed Map Tacks itself, please take it.[/b] The whole source is here, no attribution needed and no permission to ask for:

[url=https://github.com/bopielka/detailed-map-tacks-fixes]https://github.com/bopielka/detailed-map-tacks-fixes[/url]

I would rather this mod became unnecessary than kept existing.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]UI only.[/b] No rules, values or balance are changed. It does not affect saved games and can be removed mid-save.
[*] Loads after Detailed Map Tacks by design, and changes what is running rather than replacing any of its files.
[/list]

[h2]Credits[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Detailed Map Tacks[/b] is by [b]wltk[/b]. This mod builds on it - it does not include, fork or redistribute it. All credit for map tacks in Civilization VII goes there.
[/list]
